  "id": "decussation",
  "term": "decussation",
  "definition": "Decussation is the crossing of nerve fibre pathways in the central nervous system at the midline, so that a pathway ends in centers of different levels on the opposite side. In this historical usage, it is contrasted with a commissure, which is taken to link corresponding centers.",
